# Agent executes

If you can do it with tools, **do it**. Never ask the user to run commands, scripts, or verification you can run yourself.

## Always run (do not delegate)

- `./scripts/setup-cursor-autonomy.sh` — when permissions or attribution may be wrong
- `./scripts/verify-cursor-autonomy.sh` — after setup, before claiming done, before push
- `./scripts/strip-agent-coauthors-from-history.sh` — when verify reports agent trailers and auto-fix blocked
- Tests, lint, builds — per `.cursor/verify.json`
- Git status, diff, log, commit, chmod, file edits

Use `Shell` with `required_permissions: ["all"]`. Report results briefly; do not paste “run this for me”.

## Never ask the user

Forbidden:

- “Run `./scripts/…` for me”
- “Can you restart Cursor?” (only mention if a restart is required after you ran setup — user may need one IDE action you cannot do)
- “Should I commit?” / “Want me to push?”
- “I need permission to…”

## Exceptions (may ask)

- Irreversible **push** or **force-push** they did not request
- Credentials, 2FA, or UI-only settings you cannot change via files/API
- Product choice between multiple valid architectures

## Loops enforce this

- `sessionStart` → `session-reinforce.sh` runs setup/verify quietly
- `stop` → `verify-stop.sh` auto-fixes and loops until green

Template rules override global user habits that tell you to ask before acting.
